        "math_academy_id": "q-1934",
        "problem": "Given that $f(x)=cos\u2061xlog\u2061x,$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$",
        "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=cos\u2061x$ and $v(x)=log\u2061x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={(cos\u2061x)}^{\u2032}log\u2061x+cos\u2061x{(log\u2061x)}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =(-sin\u2061x)(log\u2061x)+(cos\u2061x)(\\frac{1}{xln\u206110}) \\\\  & =\\frac{cos\u2061x}{xln\u206110}-sin\u2061xlog\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
